# L §2.3 (writer 8): `within` is gone with HOLE-STALE; lastx = "last" "(" ref "," expr ")" and a price is
# `ref | "last" "(" ref ")"`. A bound on a reading's age is a rule that tests since (L §4.6). `within` after a
# last(...) read is no clause of it: LOAD-PARSE.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit EUR: currency minor 0.01

input px[u in currencies]: num PLN/u reading
input max_age: int

ask q4: last(px[EUR], 2026-03-10) within max_age
=== expect
refused: LOAD-PARSE ...
